      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Scholars argue that linking IQ and standardized tests to \"merit\" conflates innate ability with sociocultural advantage. These tests often reflect access to resources, quality of schooling, and cultural capital, which are themselves products of social class. Therefore, what appears as meritocratic success is often evidence of systemic inequality being reproduced through biased metrics. This perspective critiques meritocracy as a narrative that masks underlying structural power imbalances.",
